vessel-aquila-name = Aquila assault shuttle
vessel-aquila-desc = A reliable Imperial lander for carrying soldiers, officers and sacred cargo under enemy fire. Its compact hull and simple auxiliary power plant keep it serviceable far from a full shipyard.

vessel-arvus-name = Arvus lighter
vessel-arvus-desc = A humble but dependable Imperial utility craft. It carries people, ammunition and provisions between ships with the stubborn reliability expected of an Imperial workhorse.

vessel-ravenwh40k-name = Raven transport
vessel-ravenwh40k-desc = A light Imperial transport with room for a small crew and useful cargo. Its simple systems are easy to maintain, making the Raven a common sight among frontier captains.

vessel-intrepidwh40k-name = Intrepid-class light cruiser
vessel-intrepidwh40k-desc = A light cruiser built for Imperial patrols and long service in the void. The Intrepid combines a formidable broadside with enough living space to sustain its crew far from friendly worlds.

vessel-cobrawh40k-name = Cobra-class destroyer
vessel-cobrawh40k-desc = A fast Imperial destroyer built to strike first and withdraw before the enemy can respond. The Cobra trades endurance for speed, torpedoes and a powerful forward attack.

vessel-perditionwh40k-name = Perdition-class light cruiser
vessel-perditionwh40k-desc = A Kasballica cruiser whose Low Gothic name is a warning. Its compact hull concentrates devastating firepower, making it a favourite of captains who expect negotiations to end in a boarding action.

vessel-swordwh40k-name = Sword-class assault corvette
vessel-swordwh40k-desc = A Kasballica assault corvette designed to close the distance and deliver accurate fire. The Sword is fast and aggressive, but unforgiving of a captain who commits to an attack too soon.

vessel-claymorewh40k-name = Claymore-class corvette
vessel-claymorewh40k-desc = A frontier corvette built around a heavy prow battery. The Claymore rewards carefully planned attack runs and punishes anyone who lets an enemy reach its flanks.

vessel-falchionwh40k-name = Falchion-class frigate
vessel-falchionwh40k-desc = A Kasballica frigate for convoy escort and hunting isolated targets. The Falchion combines speed, armour and varied weaponry rather than relying on a single trick.

vessel-desolatorwh40k-name = Desolator-class Adeptus Astartes strike cruiser
vessel-desolatorwh40k-desc = A formidable Adeptus Astartes strike vessel. The Desolator carries assault forces directly to the front, where heavy armour and precise fire can decide a clash before it becomes a war.

vessel-arkmechanicus-name = Ark Mechanicus “Covenant of the Omnissiah”
vessel-arkmechanicus-desc = An Ark Mechanicus carrying workshops, explorers and the sacred machines of a forge world. Vast and cumbersome, it can supply an expedition long after smaller ships have exhausted their stores.

vessel-miningarvus-name = Arvus mining lighter
vessel-miningarvus-desc = A stripped-down Arvus fitted with prospecting equipment. An inexpensive, practical vessel for a captain still learning to tell valuable asteroids from worthless rocks.

vessel-miningtier2-name = Prospector Mk. II mining cutter
vessel-miningtier2-desc = A second-generation mining cutter with a stronger reactor and room for a full survey team. Its reinforced hull can work deposits that would tear an entry-level lighter apart.

vessel-miningtier3-name = Mechanicus Prospector Mk. III mining vessel
vessel-miningtier3-desc = A heavy mining vessel maintained according to the rites of the Mechanicus. Its power and equipment can open rich deposits while sheltering its small crew from the void.
